# nr-office-design-composition: what the wiring applies for the composition system, the design system and the native
# design of the crate mixdog-office-design.
# (No protocol rows, no daemon service, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no Cargo edge: the modules are pure and use only
# dependencies the crate already has - mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, serde_json. They have no caller yet.)

# 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-design/src/lib.rs, the list of modules (kept sorted by the neighbours already
#    there): add `pub mod composition;` after the line `pub mod art_direction;`, and add
#    `pub mod design_system;` after the line `pub mod creative_director;`, and add `pub mod native_design;` after the
#    line `pub mod discipline;`. The crate doc comment sentence "... and the one reading of a preset table
#    (`table_input`)." gains: ", the composition planner (`composition`), the expansion of an operation list and the
#    PDF design (`design_system`) and the native design receipt (`native_design`)". The modules read the crate-private
#    helpers `prop`, `opt_prop`, `text`, `first_text`, `first_truthy` and `array_of` that lib.rs already defines.

# 2. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; after "office-colour" ... i.e. at the
#    place "office-composition" sorts to):
    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-composition.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-composition/MANIFEST.json",
